The file damage.json derives in part from D2Foundry's Oracle Engine at
commit dcd0c7d302b056ffbb532edcb711d724a17ca8c1 of
https://github.com/d2foundry/oracle_engine. Each value that derives from
Oracle Engine names the source "oracle" in damage.json. The health of a
Guardian comes from src/weapons/ttk_calc.rs. The reload scale of the
Rapid-Fire Frame comes from src/perks/other_perks.rs, and the ramp of
Target Lock comes from src/perks/year_5_perks.rs. The file damage.go
ports the math of src/weapons/ttk_calc.rs and the magazine loop of
src/weapons/dps_calc.rs to Go.

Each frame in damage.json names one source for its damage and one for
its firing times. The damage and the firing times with the source
"oracle" come from build_resources/weapon_formulas.json. That file
stores the precision damage of a frame as a scale. The precision damage
is the body damage times the sum of crit_mult / 51 and 1.5, and
damage.json holds the product, rounded to a thousandth. The other
damage and firing times of the frames are the values that Bungie's
patch notes state, and their source names the update of those notes.

